# Keeping the journal in step with Poggy Fishing

The journal keeps its own copy of the fish list. Poggy Fishing decides what is caught; the journal only shows and records it.

## What must match

| Journal | Must match in Poggy Fishing |
|---|---|
| The fish's id (the key) | The same id in the **Fish** list |
| Name | The fish's name, so players see one name |
| Item (icon) | The fish's item, so the picture matches |
| Active hours | The fish's hours, so the journal tells the truth |

A catch whose id is not in the journal is **not recorded**.

## What is display only

- **Price shown**: the price and catch value in the journal. It changes nothing else.
- **Size**: the sidebar group.
- **Species**: which lore page opens.
- **Lightest / Heaviest**: the weight range shown.

## After changing a fish in Poggy Fishing

1. Open `/poggy`, pick **Poggy Fishing Journal**, then **Fish**.
2. Find the fish by name.
3. Copy over the name, item and hours.
4. Save and restart the journal.

## Map pins and lore

The water pins, water descriptions and species lore are built into the script and cannot be edited.
Pin colours per water type are on the **Appearance** tab, under **Map pin colours**.
